<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Build Settings -->
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <SonarQubeTestProject>False</SonarQubeTestProject>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>True</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Package Info -->
    <Version>2.0.0</Version>
    <Title>Portamical.Core.Formatting</Title>
    <Authors>CsabaDu</Authors>
    <Company>CsabaDu</Company>
    <Description>Extensible formatting infrastructure for Portamical test data framework. Provides type-specific formatters, custom formatter registry, and zero-allocation string building for human-readable test case names and diagnostic output.</Description>
    <Copyright>(c) 2026. Csaba Dudas (CsabaDu)</Copyright>

    <!-- Package Assets -->
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>

    <!-- Repository -->
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/CsabaDu/Portamical/tree/master/Portamical.Core.Formatting</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageTags>formatting; testdata; extensible; performant; zeroallocation; logging; customformat; portamical;</PackageTags>

    <!-- Release Notes -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
      v2.0.0 (2026-06-28) - Architecture Simplification &amp; API Refinement

      BREAKING CHANGES:
      - Removed generic IFormatter&lt;T&gt; interface (replaced by Formatter&lt;T&gt; base class)
        • IFormatter&lt;T&gt; with contravariant 'in T' parameter removed
        • All custom formatters must now inherit from abstract Formatter&lt;T&gt; base class
        • Eliminates interface segregation - single inheritance model
        • Migration: Change 'IFormatter&lt;T&gt;' → 'Formatter&lt;T&gt;' and inherit instead of implement
      - Deleted CustomFormatters namespace and folder structure
        • Portamical.Core.Formatting.CustomFormatters.IFormatter&lt;T&gt; → removed
        • Portamical.Core.Formatting.CustomFormatters.Model.Formatter&lt;T&gt; → removed
        • All formatter types now in root Portamical.Core.Formatting namespace

      ARCHITECTURE IMPROVEMENTS:
      - Simplified formatter type hierarchy
        • Before: IFormatter (non-generic) + IFormatter&lt;in T&gt; interface + Formatter&lt;T&gt; base class
        • After: IFormatter (non-generic) + Formatter&lt;T&gt; abstract base class
        • Reduced complexity: 3 types → 2 types
        • Clearer design: Template Method pattern without contravariance complexity
      - Consolidated namespace structure
        • All formatting types in single Portamical.Core.Formatting namespace
        • Removed nested CustomFormatters/Model folder hierarchy
        • Improved discoverability and reduced cognitive load
      - Enhanced Formatter&lt;T&gt; base class
        • Now the primary and recommended way to create custom formatters
        • Sealed IFormatter.Format(object?) implementation ensures consistent type checking
        • Simplified implementation: override single Format(T) method

      DOCUMENTATION OVERHAUL:
      - Complete XML documentation review and correction (60+ fixes)
        • Standardized all inline code tags: &lt;ch&gt; → &lt;c&gt; throughout
        • Corrected all class references: FormatterRegister → Formatter
        • Fixed all interface references: IFormatter&lt;T&gt; → Formatter&lt;T&gt;
        • Updated method references to Builder.* static members
        • Fixed cref attributes pointing to renamed/removed types
      - Enhanced API documentation
        • IFormatter: Clarified public visibility and usage patterns
        • Formatter&lt;T&gt;: Enhanced Template Method pattern documentation
        • Builder: Corrected method references and clarified maxCount parameter behavior
        • DefaultFormatter: Standardized formatting and documented tuple maxCount usage (30+ tag fixes)
      - Updated all code examples
        • Replaced IFormatter&lt;T&gt; with Formatter&lt;T&gt; in examples
        • Updated namespace references in sample code
        • Corrected registry usage examples (Formatter.* instead of FormatterRegister.*)

      TEST COVERAGE ENHANCEMENTS:
      - Added 12 new Builder tests for maxCount parameter validation
        • Tests for maxCount values: 1, 2, 3, 5, 8
        • Fast path vs fallback behavior verification
        • Custom separator with various maxCount values
        • Null handling with different maxCount settings
        • Default maxCount behavior validation
      - Added 8 new tuple formatting tests
        • Tuples with 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8 elements
        • Mixed type tuples with maxCount: 8
        • Null element handling in tuples
        • Both Tuple and ValueTuple coverage
      - Test results: 225 total tests, 0 failures
        • BuilderTests: 89/89 passed (77 → 89)
        • DefaultFormatterTests: 136/136 passed (128 → 136)

      CODE QUALITY:
      - Removed contravariance complexity
        • 'in T' variance eliminated - simpler type relationships
        • No more contravariant interface tests needed
        • Easier to understand and maintain
      - Improved test coverage alignment
        • Updated CustomFormatterTests to test Formatter&lt;T&gt; base class
        • Removed contravariance-specific test cases
        • All tests passing with simplified architecture
      - Documentation accuracy improvements
        • Builder.JoinWithComma XML docs clarified for configurable maxCount
        • DefaultFormatter.Format(ITuple) explains maxCount: 8 rationale
        • Fixed cref attribute for JoinWithComma method signature

      MIGRATION GUIDE (v1.x → v2.0):

      1. Update custom formatter declarations:
         Before: public class MyFormatter : IFormatter&lt;MyType&gt;
         After:  public class MyFormatter : Formatter&lt;MyType&gt;

      2. Update namespace references (if using fully qualified names):
         Before: using Portamical.Core.Formatting.CustomFormatters;
         After:  using Portamical.Core.Formatting;

      3. Remove explicit IFormatter.Format(object?) implementations if present:
         - Formatter&lt;T&gt; base class provides this automatically
         - Only override Format(T value) in derived classes

      4. No changes needed for:
         - DefaultFormatter usage
         - Builder utility methods
         - Format method signatures
         - Registry behavior or thread-safety

      BENEFITS:
      - Simpler API surface: Fewer types to learn and understand
      - Single inheritance model: Clear extension point via Formatter&lt;T&gt;
      - Flat namespace: Better IDE auto-completion and discoverability
      - Consistent naming: Formatter for both static registry and base class
      - Better documentation: Corrected and standardized across all files
      - Comprehensive test coverage: maxCount parameter fully validated
      - Maintained performance: Zero-allocation formatting still intact

      FILES CHANGED:
      - Deleted: CustomFormatters/IFormatter.cs (131 lines)
      - Deleted: CustomFormatters/Model/Formatter.cs (258 lines)
      - Modified: Formatter.cs - generic Formatter&lt;T&gt; base class transferred from deleted file (258 lines), documentation updates
      - Modified: IFormatter.cs - made public (14 changes)
      - Modified: Builder.cs - documentation updates for maxCount parameter
      - Modified: DefaultFormatter.cs - documentation updates for tuple maxCount usage
      - Updated: README.md file
      - Updated: CustomFormatterTests.cs - aligned with new architecture
      - Added: BuilderTests - 12 new maxCount parameter tests
      - Added: DefaultFormatterTests - 8 new tuple formatting tests

      VALIDATION:
      - ✓ All builds successful (Debug/Release)
      - ✓ Zero XML documentation warnings
      - ✓ All unit tests passing (225/225)
      - ✓ Backward compatibility in behavior (API signatures changed)
      - ✓ Performance characteristics unchanged
    </PackageReleaseNotes>

    <!-- Package Generation -->
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageOutputPath>$(OutputPath)</PackageOutputPath>

    <!-- Symbols -->
    <IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    <!-- Documentation -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\icon.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\LICENSE.txt">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
